Subject: [PATCH] glamor: drain stale GL errors before probing texture formats

24.1 added a glGetError() check after the 1x1 probe glTexImage2D in
glamor_add_format(). On ANGLE an earlier call leaves an error pending, so the
depth-8 (a8) format was dropped to software, which breaks Render glyph
drawing. Clear pending errors first.

diff -ruN xwayland-24.1.13/glamor/glamor.c xwayland-24.1.13.patched/glamor/glamor.c
--- xwayland-24.1.13/glamor/glamor.c
+++ xwayland-24.1.13.patched/glamor/glamor.c
@@ -464,6 +464,10 @@
         glBindTexture(GL_TEXTURE_2D, tex);
         glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, GL_NEAREST);
         glTexParameteri(GL_TEXTURE_2D, GL_TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, GL_NEAREST);
+        /* Drain errors left over from earlier setup (ANGLE leaves one
+         * pending), so the check below only sees glTexImage2D's own. */
+        for (int i = 0; i < 16 && glGetError() != GL_NO_ERROR; i++)
+            ;
         glTexImage2D(GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, internalformat, 1, 1, 0,
                      format, type, NULL);
         if (glGetError() != GL_NO_ERROR)
